# Netlify redirect rules for regentparking.ca (this marketing site's own
# apex domain — a separate Netlify project from the app itself).
#
# These are 301 redirects, not proxies: a visitor going to
# regentparking.ca/<tenant> is sent to the real tenant subdomain
# (<tenant>.regentparking.ca) and the URL bar changes. That keeps
# index.html's resolveTenantSubdomain() as the single source of truth for
# who a visit belongs to, instead of two different URLs quietly serving
# the same content (which risks going stale if one side changes).
#
# Add one line per tenant when you create a new one in Platform Admin.
# This file lives in the marketing site's own project, so a new line here
# needs its own git push/redeploy of regent-parking-marketing/ — adding
# the tenant in Platform Admin and adding the custom domain in Netlify
# don't touch this file automatically.

/dueast    https://dueast.regentparking.ca/         301
/dueast/*  https://dueast.regentparking.ca/:splat   301
